# Copy to deploy/uat/.env (gitignored) and fill in. Names only; no defaults for the ingress
# restriction on purpose: compose and ingress-guard.sh refuse to start while any is empty.
ITSM_UAT_IMAGE_TAG=
ITSM_UAT_SITE_ADDRESS=
# "internal" (Caddy local CA; clients must trust it) or an ACME e-mail for a public hostname.
ITSM_UAT_TLS=
# Office/VPN egress IPs or CIDRs, space separated. 0.0.0.0/0 and ::/0 are refused.
ITSM_UAT_ALLOWED_CIDRS=
ITSM_UAT_BASIC_AUTH_USER=
# Optional (defaults shown in compose.yaml):
# ITSM_UAT_HTTPS_BIND=0.0.0.0:443
# ITSM_UAT_HTTP_BIND=0.0.0.0:80
# ITSM_UAT_BACKEND_SUBNET=172.30.57.0/24
# ITSM_UAT_INGRESS_IP=172.30.57.10
# ITSM_OUTBOX_WORKER=off  (on|off) worker inside the api process. Off since CP7b: the separate
#                         `worker` service delivers; scale it with --scale worker=N.
# ITSM_DB_MAX_CONNECTIONS=10        pool per api process (1-200). Sum over all api and worker
# ITSM_WORKER_DB_MAX_CONNECTIONS=4  processes must stay below Postgres max_connections (100) minus
#                                   a reserve. See deploy/RUNBOOK-scaling.md.
# CP7d: limits shared by every api replica (Postgres). Requests per window, 1-1000000. Empty =
# default. deploy/RUNBOOK-scaling.md "Rate limit bersama".
# ITSM_LIMIT_AUTH_PER_IP_10MIN=100       sign-in attempts per client address per 10 minutes
# ITSM_LIMIT_AI_PER_USER_MIN=10          AI suggestions per user per minute
# ITSM_LIMIT_AI_PER_WORKSPACE_DAY=2000   AI suggestions per company per day (UTC)
# ITSM_LIMIT_OUTBOUND_PER_USER_10MIN=30  connection tests, sync, retries per user per 10 minutes
# ITSM_LIMIT_LOOKUP_PER_USER_MIN=60      live Jira look-ups per user per minute
# ITSM_LIMIT_WEBHOOK_PER_IP_MIN=600      Jira webhook deliveries per address per minute
# ITSM_DB_ACQUIRE_TIMEOUT_MS=3000   wait for a free pool connection (100-30000) before 503.
# ITSM_METRICS_BIND=0.0.0.0:9464   separate /metrics listener (CP7a), not published, must differ
#                                  from ITSM_BIND. See deploy/RUNBOOK-observability.md.
# Attachments are out of scope (D13): leave unset. Empty = uploads refused fail-closed (503).
# Only with the feature re-enabled AND `--profile attachments`: ITSM_CLAMD_ADDR=tcp://clamav:3310
# ITSM_CLAMD_ADDR=
# MFA (US-1.2), password mode only. Off by default (owner 2026-11-12): plain password login, no
# step-up, MFA routes 404, the three keys below are not needed. Set ITSM_MFA=on to bring it back;
# then production password mode refuses to start while any key is empty. Never commit values.
# ITSM_MFA=off   (on|off)
# Keyring (encrypts TOTP seeds and Jira/Lark credentials): NOT here. It lives in the secret file
#   secrets/itsm_keyring = key_id:base64(32 random bytes)[,key_id:...]  (empty file = no keyring;
#   keep old key ids listed while rotating, see deploy/RUNBOOK-keyring.md). check-config refuses
#   ITSM_KEYRING in this file; production refuses it as an env var.
# ITSM_KEYRING_ACTIVE=   key_id used for new seeds / credentials (not secret)
# ITSM_MFA_RECOVERY_PEPPER=   base64 of >= 32 random bytes (HMAC key for recovery codes)
# Jira/Lark integrations (CP5b). Any other value refuses to start.
# ITSM_INTEGRATIONS=          live|simulation. Empty = simulation in UAT, live in production;
#                             production refuses simulation. live needs the keyring (+ _ACTIVE):
#                             without them credentials cannot be saved (503 keyring_missing).
# ITSM_INTEGRATIONS_LAB=off   on|off. on allows http:// and private/loopback targets (test stubs
#                             only); refused in production.
# ITSM_INTEGRATIONS_TIMEOUT_MS=5000   500-8000, budget of one provider call (no redirects).
# Company SSO (CP5c). Only with ITSM_ACCESS_MODE=password; any other value refuses to start.
# This UAT stack runs uat_superadmin, so check-config refuses sso/both here. Production setup and
# the IdP registration steps (Entra ID, Google, Keycloak): deploy/RUNBOOK-sso.md.
# ITSM_AUTH=password          password|sso|both. sso = OIDC only (password form kept for
#                             break-glass platform admins); both = OIDC and passwords.
# ITSM_PUBLIC_URL=            origin users open, e.g. https://itsm.example.co.id (required for
#                             sso/both). IdP redirect URI = <origin>/api/v1/auth/oidc/callback.
# ITSM_OIDC_LAB=off           on|off. on allows http:// and private IdP addresses (local stub
#                             IdP only); refused in production.
# Egress proxy (CP6b). compose.yaml always points the API at egress-proxy; credentials are the
# secret files secrets/egress_proxy_auth (api: user:password) and secrets/egress_proxy_htpasswd
# (proxy: user:hash), see deploy/RUNBOOK-egress.md. Allowed hosts: deploy/egress/allowlist.regex.
# ITSM_EGRESS_DNS=1.1.1.1 8.8.8.8   IPv4 resolvers the proxy uses (space separated).
